2) Wire Gauge, Color Code, and Insulation

2.1 Recommended AWG (based on current & typical run lengths)

120 V AC branch (15 A): 14 AWG THHN/THWN or MTW; 105 °C insulation; stranded.

120 V AC branch (20 A option): 12 AWG.

240 V AC 20 A branch: 12 AWG (hot/hot + ground).

Main AC bus between inverter/alt and breakers (≤30 A): 10 AWG.

12 V DC high‑current (≤30 A, ≤2 m run): 10–12 AWG (use 10 AWG if voltage drop must be <3%).

12 V DC aux (≤10 A): 14–16 AWG.

Signal/logic: 20–22 AWG twisted pairs for sensors; shielded where near magnets.


> For long runs (>2 m) or higher ambient temps, step one gauge heavier. All high‑motion areas use fine‑strand automotive TXL/GXL.



2.2 Color Code (internal standard)

AC HOT (L): Black (L1), Red (L2).

AC NEUTRAL (N): White.

AC GROUND (PE): Green/Green‑Yellow stripe.

12 V +: Red.

12 V − / Chassis return: Black.

Logic 5 V: Orange.

Signals (sensors): Blue (data), Yellow (clk), Violet (aux).

Brake/servo control: Gray.

E‑Stop loop: Pink (distinct for quick tracing).


2.3 Insulation & Looming

Use PET braided sleeving with tinned copper braid over AC bundles near the magnetic core for EMI.

Heat‑shrink at exits; adhesive‑lined in high‑vibration areas.

Strain relief: P‑clips or cushioned clamps every 200 mm.



