5) Protection & Safety Chain

Line protection: Thermal‑magnetic breakers at each outlet; main AC bus fused if upstream source > branch rating.

DC: Master ANL/Mega fuse near 12 V source (e.g., 40–60 A as calculated), plus branch fuses/breakers.

E‑Stop: Latching, mushroom switch (twist‑to‑reset) in a series loop that:

1. Drops the excitation/drive via the latching power relay (de‑energize to open).


2. Commands servo brake to engage (fail‑safe spring return if power lost).


3. Signals MCU to log fault and show red LCD alarm.



12 V port: Resettable breaker + polarity protection (Schottky/MOSFET ORing) + TVS diode.

Surge/EMI: MOVs across AC lines; RC snubbers across relay contacts; common‑mode choke on 12 V input to logic.



---

6) Control Logic (Panel)

Front‑panel devices (left→right):

1. ON/OFF Toggle (logic enable).


2. START (momentary) – energize drive/coil start up to ramp RPM.


3. SERVO BRAKE KNOB (pot) – analog setpoint to MCU for braking force.


4. E‑STOP – latching mushroom.


5. 12 V RESET – manual reset for 12 V port breaker/switch.


6. LCD Panel – V/Hz/RPM/alarms.



Functional sequence:

Power‑on: Toggle ON → MCU boots → self‑test → LCD green.

Start: Hold START → drive enables softly (slew‑rate limited) → release at target idle RPM.

Brake: Rotate knob → MCU maps setpoint to servo torque/position; closed‑loop w/ RPM feedback.

E‑Stop: Immediate coil drop, servo to full brake, LCD red, event log.


Latching Relay Wiring (excitation/drive cut):

Coil powered through E‑Stop loop and MCU OK line (series). Loss of either opens main drive feed.

Manual RESET on panel re‑arms after fault clear.



