8) Mechanical Integration

8.1 Servo‑Actuated Magnetic Brake Lever

Purpose: Apply opposing magnetic polarity to the mercury‑attached (or equivalent) magnetic rings to brake/attenuate torque.

Mechanism: Lever arm on rotary servo (metal‑gear, 25–35 kg·cm) drives a non‑magnetic linkage (G10/FR4 or 316 SS hardware) to a flux‑shunt blade positioned near the core.

Fail‑safe: Spring‑return to "brake" when power is lost (or inverse, per test preference). Select spring constant to reach full travel within <150 ms.

Stops: Soft silicone bumpers; mechanical hard‑stops to prevent over‑travel.

Shielding: Mu‑metal/permalloy shield around servo body if within 100 mm of strong fields.


Mounting Stack (left→right):
Chassis plate (4 mm Al) → Servo bracket (3 mm Al or steel, powder‑coat) → M4 rivnuts → Servo → 25T horn → Lever (G10 5 mm) → Rod‑end (M3) → Shunt blade carriage (linear guide mini‑rail).

Lever Geometry (suggested):

Lever length 40–50 mm; shunt blade travel 8–12 mm per full stroke.

Position the blade 0.5–2.0 mm clearance from ring at max brake; tune after flux mapping.


8.2 Flywheel & Magnetic Bearings

Flywheel: Dynamically balance to G 6.3 or better; include keyed hub and safety retainer.

Magnetic bearings: Ensure axial restraint via secondary thrust bearing (ceramic hybrid) to capture lift.

Run‑out: Target <0.03 mm TIR; shim as required.

Sensors: Place Hall target on a non‑ferrous standoff, radial offset 3–5 mm from sensor face.


8.3 Enclosure & Routing

Bulkheads: Pass‑through glands (IP67) for each harness; separate AC vs DC penetrations by ≥100 mm.

Cable trays: 20×40 mm internal ducts with finger slots; removable lids.

Airflow: Intake baffled; keep intakes >150 mm away from magnetic dust sources; add filter.


8.4 Fasteners & Adhesives

Fasteners: 304/316 SS; thread‑locker (blue) on vibration paths.

Epoxy (2‑part spray):

Bond magnets to acrylic fixtures.

Pot coil spools (thin coats, avoid heat soak).

Seal enclosure seams; mount LED strips.


Respect cure schedule; mask bearing journals.



